    <outline text="Nintendo begins podcasting!">
      <outline text=" Walter 	&#10;&#10;Nintendo has just begun podcasting, K9Cast has the scoop:&#10;www.k9cast.com—more-on-nintendogsnintendos-first.html &lt;http://www.k9cast.com/2005/08/more-on-nintendogsnintendos-first.html&gt;&#10;&#10;The timing of this is interesting because the Play-Yan mp3/multimedia&#10;add-on player for the Nintendo DS and GBA may see a US release date in&#10;&quot;late 2005&quot; according to wikipedia. Nintendo could be planning to turn&#10;DS and GBAs into podcast players! With over 50 million Gameboy Advance&#10;units sold that's alot of listeners!&#10;&#10;The first episode of the Nintendo Podcast is on the subject of&#10;Nintendogs, a virtual dog game (hence the interest to K9Cast).&#10;&#10;Excellent.&#10;&#10;Walter"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="Listening to a podcast story">
      <outline text=" JP Dane-Castro 	&#10;&#10;Hey Adam.  My name is JP and I have been a long time listener and fan of the Daily Source Code.  First off I would just like to say happy birthday to you and your daughter Christina, congratulations to both of you.  Second I would just like to say that a funny thing happened to me the other day. The car I was in drove under an overpass while I was listening to the latest installation of the Daily Source Code and for a split second I thought to myself &quot;oh no, I am going to lose reception&quot;.  I then immediately thought to myself &quot;wait, this is a podcast, you can't lose reception.&quot;  So there is the beauty of podcasting, being able to listen to what you want, when you want without having to worry about bad reception, or interceptions.  So Adam I just thought that I would share that little tidbit of podcasting goodness with you, I love the show and keep up the good work! "/>
    </outline>
